From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:07:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chunkio: use ftw(3) for recursive delete on QNX

cio_utils_recursive_delete() uses fts(3) from <fts.h> on POSIX systems. The
QNX SDP 8.0 has no <fts.h>, but it does have <ftw.h> with nftw() and
FTW_DEPTH/FTW_PHYS, which the Emscripten code path already uses.

Select the nftw() based implementation on QNX as well.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 lib/chunkio/src/cio_utils.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/chunkio/src/cio_utils.c b/lib/chunkio/src/cio_utils.c
index 0a63cc8..11386ca 100644
--- a/lib/chunkio/src/cio_utils.c
+++ b/lib/chunkio/src/cio_utils.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <chunkio/cio_info.h>
-#if defined(CIO_HAVE_BACKEND_FILESYSTEM) && defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#if defined(CIO_HAVE_BACKEND_FILESYSTEM) && (defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__QNXNTO__))
 #include <ftw.h>
 #elif defined(CIO_HAVE_BACKEND_FILESYSTEM) && !defined(_WIN32)
 #include <fts.h>
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ int cio_utils_recursive_delete(const char *dir)
     errno = ENOSYS;
     return CIO_ERROR;
 }
-#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__QNXNTO__)
 static int cio_utils_remove_entry(const char *path, const struct stat *st,
                                   int type, struct FTW *walk)
 {
